{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>To the camp, the one.</b> One may say: [it was devoted to] one of the Matriarchs. And the remaining camp shall be לפליטה, so that Esau would not think I have two camps. Another interpretation: while Esau is fighting the one camp, there is time for the remaining camp לפליטה to flee; or after he strikes the first camp, he and his men will be weary and exhausted, and the remaining camp shall be לפליטה, not weary, and will fight them and kill them." "<b>Ha-machaneh ha-achat, והכהו.</b> [Anything that has no spirit of life is sometimes called in masculine form and sometimes in feminine form.]"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:03.551298358Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}